:option {:value "256226"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "256235"} "Kayak Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "256241"} "Kayak Fours, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "256247"} "Canadian Singles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "256253"} "Canadian Singles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "256259"} "Canadian Doubles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "256265"} "Canadian Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "256292"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "256298"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "256304"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "255441"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "255581"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "255675"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "255783"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "255925"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "256068"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "256317"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258743"} "2008"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/159"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "27 September –  1 October 2000"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/753"} "Sydney International Regatta Centre, Penrith, New South Wales"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/256204"} "31 from 31 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Hungary had won the men’s K-1 500 at the last three editions of the World Championships, most recently with " [:a {:href "/athletes/90208"} "Ákos Vereckei"] ", its entry for the event at the 2000 Summer Olympics. " [:a {:href "/athletes/9213"} "Petar Merkov"] " of Bulgaria was the most recent European Champion and World runner-up, while Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/10397"} "Knut Holmann"] " the 1996 runner-up and 1992 bronze medalist, was the only returning Olympic medalist. " [:a {:href "/athletes/8965"} "Javier Correa"] " of Argentina, meanwhile, had taken the title at the 1999 Pan American Games. Vereckei, Merkov, and Correa won their opening heats, but Holmann was defeated by " [:a {:href "/athletes/10494"} "Grzegorz Kotowicz"] " of Poland, the 1997 and 1999 World runner-up and bronze medalist respectively. Holmann was again bested in the semi-finals, this time by Vereckei, while Merkov captured his heat and Kotowicz came in third behind Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/9949"} "Lutz Liwowski"] ", the 1998 World bronze medalist, and Spain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/9489"} "Jovino González"] ". Correa placed sixth in the latter heat and was eliminated. " [:a {:href "/athletes/90212"} "Michael Kolganov"] " of Israel, the 1998 World runner-up, had a fantastic start in the final and sizeable lead through the first half of the course, but was eventually passed by Holmann and Merkov  and thus settled for bronze. This was Israel’s first and, as of 2012, only Olympic canoeing medal, and was somewhat of a consolation for the one that he had missed by 0.042 seconds the previous day in the K-1 1000. Holmann and Merkov, meanwhile, had managed to repeat their performances from that event in the K-1 500."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/10397"} "Knut